{% doc %}
  The MCP tools this module offers, in the shape pos-module-mcp's registry
  expects: { name, path }, where path is the tool directory whose manifest
  partial declares it.

  A host app that installs pos-module-mcp concatenates this into its own
  app/lib/mcp/registry.liquid. The engine reads its registry from that fixed
  app path, so a module cannot register itself — every tool an instance serves
  is named in one reviewed app file, and dropping these files on disk does
  nothing on its own.

  Names carry the support_ prefix: tool names are global to an instance's
  registry, and this module ships into apps that may serve their own.
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign reads = 'support_search_tickets,support_read_ticket,support_find_customer,support_queue_overview,support_saved_replies' | split: ','
  # Every write tool sets requires_approval, so the engine stores the
  # arguments and runs the handler only once a person approves.
  assign writes = 'support_add_note,support_set_priority,support_change_status,support_snooze_ticket,support_assign_ticket,support_reply_to_customer' | split: ','
  assign names = reads | concat: writes
  assign tools = []
  for name in names
    assign entry = { "name": name }
    assign entry['path'] = 'modules/support/mcp/tools/' | append: name
    assign tools = tools | array_add: entry
  endfor
  return tools
%}
